      "message": "I\u0027m still learning myself when to use `std::span`. I found [this reddit post](https://www.reddit.com/r/cpp_questions/comments/18l72qe/returning_const_stdvector_vs_stdspan_in_getters/) interesting. I think I find myself leaning towards returning a const ref to the underlying type to be preferred, mainly because it doesn\u0027t limit the API the caller can use, and `std::span` isn\u0027t totally free (although I\u0027m sure it\u0027s mostly negligible).",
